        <p>FURNITURE BY GILLOVir. FURNITURE BY OGDEN. FURNITURE BY LAMB. FURNITURE BY MAPLE. FURNITURE BY SHOOLBRED. FURNITURE BY GARNETT. dr.c., The extensive alterations nece,sitated by continued in- crease of business haviog now been almost completed, the Proprietors have pleasure in informing their old-established " clientel " and the rublic generaly that the increased Exhibitian Space in their Showrooms (opposite all Sainte' Church) has enabled them to stock and display an enorm- onsly added Qiaantity of FURNITURE—both new and Second-band—so that their Customers have now a Collection to choose from, which it is not too much to say is second to none in the United Kingdom. Whilst, of course, the Market is being flooded with new Modern Furniture, there scarcely was a time when High-class, t, econd-hand, Durable and Handsome SUITES were more difficult to obtain. But ever on the alert, the first in o a field, we are glad to say tbst we have been successful in securing one of the rarest and completest Collections of every variety of Furniture ever offeted to the public since we entered the Trade. These com- prise The Household Furniture of a Wesleynn Minister near Manchester, wh has recently been appointed to the Foreign Missions. 2. The establishment of a leading heavy weight jockey, who is about to start as a North Country Trainer. 3. The Household Effects of an ex-24.P. in Staffordshire, who has been ordered abroad on account of in.. health. 4. Seven Houses of Furniture from Suburban Villas and Mansions sold under writs of " fieri fade!," and purciased by GOLDSTONE and SONS ; the whoic compris- ing the most Magnificent and Elaborate Selection ever seen in Manchester (part already spoken for) and Now on 'View. "Chef d'reuvres "by the most Celebrated Makers. Furni- ture in Chippendale, Sheraton and Antique Oak. Furniture in Ash, Birch, Maple, Walnut, Rosewood, and Mahogany. £10.003 OF NEWLY-ADDED STOCK. Now on offer at nearly one-halt its original value. Railway Fares Paid to Country Customers. Catalogues Free on Ap plication. THOSE ABOUT .TO MARRY _</p>
        <p>and those who contemplate adding to their present Stock ef Furniture are specially invited to pay an early visit to the Manchester Louvre (opposite All Saints' Church). Advice gratis on the choice and selection of</p>
