        <p>£lO 10s. Solid Walnut DRAWING-ROOM SUITE, In very. lostly velvet and plush border. The Suite comprises the full seven pieces, and we without doubt a marvel of cheap- nese at £3O; our price only £lO 108. £l2 12s. Solid Walnut lIIIIDIfOOII SUITE, by Ogden, consisting of large wardrobe, with bevelled silver plate in dam, plenty of room for hangings, and large drawers below ; pair of very massive toilet tables, wito swing glass to dress- ing table; and washstand, marble slab and tile back • three cane chairs, towel airer, and redestal combined. This suite konestly worth £4O. £6 15.. ; cost when new £2O. The handsomest pair .of TOILET TABLES in Manchester; all solid Walnut, large swing bevelled crystal glass, surmounted by jewel drawers and cupboards. The WASIISIAND, with marble slab, tile back and bevelled mirr( r, all braes handled.</p>
        <p>£2 15s. The mast complete SST of FIRS BRASSES in England, consisting of handsome solid brass curb, all tut and well made. pair of massive dogs ; the heavy bras ;is% with beautifully met and chaste handles and brass stop, aft en suite, was never made for less than £lO,</p>
        <p>£ll, worth £S. Handsome BRASS CURB. PAIR of Heavy FIRE DOGS, SET of FIRE BRASSES, all to match. £lB 18s. Very good Second-hand ItHDHOOM bUITE, in solid walnut ; the usual complement of pieces ; very hand- somely carved and repolished like new. Usual price £37 10s. £lO 10s., worth £3O. Very handsome Chippendale DRAWING ROOM SUITE, in expensive Genoa velvet,nicely. carved frames and well finished. 1 heSuite consists of settee, pair of two ea•y chairs, and four occasional chatre. £25, cost 1:65. A Grand 1-arlram in a Second-hand Solid Walnut DINING-ROOM SUL IE, by Maple, in real Crocodile leather, all hair-stuffrri.</p>
        <p>£2 lhs. Maseive DINING-TABLE, to seat 12 persons, a solid wood, very heavy legs, and extends to sfl. ; worth £5. £75, cost £260. The Fioest BliDltoo3f SUITE outside London. Space does not permit to give anything like a true desCrlption. Anyone uniting to have a suite that will be as a heirloom to the family should see this suite. Nothing bet-- ter can be mad, nor obtained.</p>
        <p>£l5, worth £5O. Complete House of SECOND-HAND FURNITUE, consisting of parlour, kitchen, and two bed- rooms, everything complete. £5O, cost £ISJ. he Ent,re CONTENTS of a SIX-ROOMED HOUSE to be disposed of, write for particulars.</p>
        <p>BEDSTEADS.</p>
