      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-11-30_WidnesExaminer_art0078" n="art0078">
        <head>WESTON.</head>
        <p>WESTON.</p>
        <p>PARISH COUNCIL MEETING.— A special meeting of this Council was held on Friday evening, when there were present Messrs. A. G. Guest, S. Savage, James Tudor,D, Basnett, John Vose, R. R. Clarke, and J. Collier (clerk). The clerk read a letter from the Rev. Canon Wood, ex- pressing regret that his absence in London prevented his being present, and Mr. Guest was voted to the chair.— The report of the committee as to their interview with a sub-committee of the District Council with reference to the night soil question,was read. It had been proposed by Mr. Chadwick and seconded by Mr. Aaron, that the Parish Council Committee visit the farmers,and request them to send in tenders for a night soil deposit bank in each yard.—The clerk stated that in order to carry out the recommendation of the committee tenders had been sought and three had been received.—Mr. Vose said the suggestion would mean an increase of £lO a year on the rates. The deposit banks would not get them out of the difficulty.—On the motion of Mr. Clarke, seconded by Mr. Basnett. it was decided to recommend the Die- trict Council to accept the tender of Mr. Thomas Ford, for £5 for Weaver Ward; and on the proposition of Mr. Savage seconded by Mr. Clarke, it was recommended that the one sent in for Mr. John Jeffs for £.5 for the Weaver Ward be accepted. There voted in favour of the proposition Messrs. Savage, Clarke, and basnett ; and Mr. 13a3 against,the other members present refrain.. ing from voting. Tux NEW CHIIRCH.—The Vicar of Runcorn in his monthly letter to his parishioners. says—" At length I have recived the final decision of the Incorporated Church Building Society, and it is pleasant to be able to announce that they have promised on the completion of the new church at Weston, to pay towards it the sum of £85."</p>
        <p>WESLEYAN BAND OF 130 PH.—The first of the winter series of entainments was given by this society in the Wesleyan Scho Iroom en Tuesday night,under the presi. dency of Miss Allen (Warrington). There was a large audience of adult people present. Miss Dutton (Moore), in the 'course of the evening gave an address. Misses Edith Smith, Mort, Lear, Aldridge, Jones, and Mr, Fitton, took part in the programme of songs. recitations &amp;c. On the motion of Mr. Thomas Ford, seconded by Mr. W. Dunbabin, a hearty vote at thanks was passed to Miss Allen and Miss Dutton.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-11-30_WidnesExaminer_art0079" n="art0079">
        <head>COLLISION ON TFIE CANAL NEIR RIM° RN.</head>
        <p>COLLISION ON TFIE CANAL NEIR RIM° RN.</p>
        <p>SINKING OF A FLAT.</p>
        <p>r r</p>
        <p>51.1t6</p>
        <p>On Thursday night a collision occurred on the Bridgewater Canal near Astmore Wharfe. It appears that a flat of Messrs. Thomason, of Liver- pool, was proceeding on her way to Runcorn when on nearing Astmore Wharf° the narrow boat "Vulture," loaded with china clay, and below; ing to the Andertou Company, collided with her. The flat proceeded a little distance and then sank. The crew were fortunately enabled to jump on the tow- ing path. Very little damage was done to the ; Vulture, awl she was able to proceed ou bet journey. Arrangements are being made by Mr. Wiswall, of the Manchester Ship Canal Company. ! for the immediate raising of the flat which luckily was " light "at the time.</p>
        <p>PROPOSED WIDENING OF TUB RAILWAY A.T RDNCORN.</p>
        <p>' it IN stated that the'London and North-Western Railway company are promoting in the next sea- in of Parliament a 13111 to empower tbem,amongst other thingc,to widen their grand Junction railway at Ituncom, Little Sankey, and Warrington, No detai/s are at present available, but it is understood that this will include the widening of Runcorn Bridge. At present there are four sets ot metals from :Ditto» to Liverpool, and it is surmised, in. usu Cly well informed quarters, that it is in con- templatioh to continue trieBe four lines on to Acton Bridge Junction,</p>
      </div>
