        <p>The usual monthly meeting of this Board was held on Tuesday evening, in the Board-room, Great Sankey, the chair being occupied by Mr. 11. Bate. There were also present—the Rev. E. S. Jackson, and Messrs. Fairclough, Wright, W. D. Jeans, jun. (clerk), and G. Clarke (school-master).—The minutes of the previous meeting were read and confirmed.—The Clerk read theannual report,which showed that discipline in the mixed schools had been good throughout. The upper classes received commendation for their work, although the arith- metic and reading needed careful attention inmost of the standards. The infant classes also seemed to have had much care bestowed on their instruction, reading and writing being their best subjects. The two pupil teachers who submitted themselves for examination had passed successfully. Form 9 of the School Board, which showed the expenditure of the whole years, denoted that only 11d. had been used by the schools during that length of time. There had been £291 193. 6d. received by the School Board from the Education Department.—The Clerk informed the Board tha,t there were several cheques to be presented that night for salaries, &amp;c., and there was an additional one that month for 45., the amount due to one of the monitresses.—The attend- ance officer had proceeded against several persons for the irregular attendance of their children at school, but a great improvement had been noticed in each case.—The other businessCwas of a routine character. ad a =ME lit,</p>
